5714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526383 1083 #uuid "d32cc603-e58c-5b00-a8b9-0a073ffc01e3" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526384 1080 "x^{2}-y^{2}=\\frac{11}{2}" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526384 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526384 1083 #uuid "d97f9dc5-21b6-5ee0-a46c-0f9f54098a9e" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526385 1068 #edb/ref 17592186526381 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526385 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526385 1071 "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526385 1072 #uuid "eaf5e3f7-8e64-5b18-999b-2cd25904a7b4" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526385 1074 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta.$ We can do this using the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.$$\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta\\\\x^2&=(\\frac{11}{2}\\cos\\theta)^2\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta\\\\y^2&=(\\frac{11}{2}\\sin\\theta)^2\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using the identity, we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}x^2+y^2&=\\frac{121}{4}\\cos^2\\theta+\\frac{121}{4}\\sin^2\\theta\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}(1)\\\\&=\\frac{121}{4}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^{2}+y^{2}=\\frac{121}{4}.$" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526386 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186087786.py" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true] [17592186526386 1169 #uuid "a54d8bb4-25f4-5f81-89b1-02014a4fe86f" 13194139535714 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids